       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5 to 10 mg. A 50 mg dose could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, the effects could last for days.\n\nCould you check whether one of these was intended?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a common starting dose.\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for frail patients or those who need a lower dose.\n\nIf 50 mg is correct, for example because of an unusual protocol, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
